# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend (Next.js) environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and adjust as needed:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the JavaScript bundle at BUILD time and
# are visible to anyone using the site. Never put secrets here — this file is
# committed, and the values ship to the browser regardless.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- API (required) --------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the backend API, including the /api prefix that the backend
# mounts globally. No trailing slash.
#
# This is the ONLY env var the frontend reads. It is used in two places:
#   - src/lib/api/http.ts       -> the axios instance baseURL
#   - src/components/layout/header.tsx -> the SSE alerts stream
#
# Leaving it unset does NOT fail loudly: axios falls back to relative paths
# against the Next.js origin, so every API call 404s against the frontend
# instead of reaching the backend. Always set it explicitly.
#
# Local dev (backend on port 4000):
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL="http://localhost:4000/api"
#
# Production example:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL="https://api.your-domain.com/api"
